       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want the original order, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. I'd strongly advise against that."
      }
